WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:07.630
<v Speaker 1>You are warmly welcome to this deep dive into a pretty harsh but profoundly transformative reality.

2
00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:09.790
<v Speaker 2>Yeah, harsh is definitely the word I'd use.

3
00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:15.230
<v Speaker 1>I mean, I want you to imagine spending your entire life following every single rule of your religion perfectly.

4
00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:17.710
<v Speaker 2>Just doing everything exactly by the book.

5
00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:18.590
<v Speaker 1>Exactly.

6
00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:28.750
<v Speaker 1>You observe the rituals, you memorize the texts, you do all the physical motions prescribed to you, do absolutely everything asked of you by the visible tradition, and then

7
00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:35.310
<v Speaker 1>you're told that despite all of that flawless observance, you're still operating at the spiritual level of a beast.

8
00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:37.270
<v Speaker 2>Which is just a staggering thought.

9
00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:40.110
<v Speaker 2>It fundamentally shakes how we understand religious practice.

10
00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:40.830
<v Speaker 1>It really does.

11
00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:48.990
<v Speaker 1>But that is the exact unyielding scenario we are unpacking today from a remarkable text known as the Master and the Disciple.

12
00:00:49.310 --> 00:00:51.470
<v Speaker 1>It originates from 10th century Yemen.

13
00:00:51.470 --> 00:00:52.830
<v Speaker 2>And it doesn't hold back at all.

14
00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:53.710
<v Speaker 1>Not even a little.

15
00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:58.830
<v Speaker 1>What this text does is lay out a strict foundational architecture of knowledge.

16
00:00:59.230 --> 00:01:02.350
<v Speaker 1>It doesn't just divide knowledge into the known and the unknown.

17
00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:04.590
<v Speaker 1>It presents a three-layer structure.

18
00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:08.670
<v Speaker 1>So you have the outer aspect, the inner aspect, and the inner of the inner.

19
00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:17.830
<v Speaker 2>And what makes this geometry so compelling and frankly so demanding is that these three dimensions map perfectly onto 3 levels of creatures.

20
00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:20.670
<v Speaker 1>Right, which are beasts, humans, and angels.

21
00:01:21.070 --> 00:01:27.790
<v Speaker 1>And before we get into the mechanics of that mapping, I want to plant the core thesis that anchors this entire system.

22
00:01:27.790 --> 00:01:29.950
<v Speaker 1>This is the absolute spine of the text.

23
00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:31.310
<v Speaker 1>The ladder is real.

24
00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:34.110
<v Speaker 1>The highest rung cannot be transferred, only earned.

25
00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:41.430
<v Speaker 2>And just to clarify our lens for this deep dive before we go further, we are looking at a classical Ismaili reading of this architecture.

26
00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:43.070
<v Speaker 1>That's A crucial positionality note.

27
00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:54.430
<v Speaker 2>Yeah, because this framework has significant overlap with the broader Sufi tradition and its dedicated search for inward meaning, but it maintains a very sharp structured distinction from the Sunni juristic difference.

28
00:01:55.150 --> 00:01:58.350
<v Speaker 2>We're examining a highly specific spiritual geometry here.

29
00:01:58.430 --> 00:01:58.750
<v Speaker 1>We are.

30
00:01:58.910 --> 00:02:03.390
<v Speaker 2>But looking at that architecture, as a seeker, I have an immediate crisis with it.

31
00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:07.150
<v Speaker 2>Like the disciple in the text experiences this firsthand.

32
00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:07.870
<v Speaker 1>Tell me about that.

33
00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:08.750
<v Speaker 2>I mean.

34
00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:15.710
<v Speaker 2>I can easily understand an outer layer and an inner layer, but does the inner actually have an innermost dimension?

35
00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:25.150
<v Speaker 2>And more importantly, if this highest angelic rung exists, is it actually climbable by a human being or is it permanently sealed off from human reach?

36
00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:26.830
<v Speaker 1>That is the big question, isn't it?

37
00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:27.310
<v Speaker 2>Is.

38
00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:30.470
<v Speaker 2>And frankly, I have to challenge the necessity of climbing at all.

39
00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:34.950
<v Speaker 2>Like, why isn't mere observance of the rules sufficient?

40
00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:36.950
<v Speaker 1>You mean just following the visible practices?

41
00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:38.710
<v Speaker 2>Yeah, let's say a person observes all the

42
00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:43.630
<v Speaker 2>visible practices, lives an orderly life, fulfills their communal obligations perfectly.

43
00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:45.710
<v Speaker 2>Why do they need to seek out these hidden layers?

44
00:02:45.710 --> 00:02:47.110
<v Speaker 2>Why is the outer not enough?

45
00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:52.350
<v Speaker 1>Well, because treating mere observance as enough completely collapses the latter.

46
00:02:52.750 --> 00:03:00.230
<v Speaker 1>The text counters this assumption with a very stark, almost clinical warning, if you know only the outer aspect of the physical world.

47
00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:02.510
<v Speaker 2>Just reciting names and observing rituals.

48
00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:03.550
<v Speaker 1>Yeah, exactly.

49
00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:10.030
<v Speaker 1>If you do that without ever asking what those things point to, you leave yourself operating at the level of beasts.

50
00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:14.510
<v Speaker 1>The tradition calls this strictly visible surface, Zahir.

51
00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:19.950
<v Speaker 2>That is a brutally harsh categorization for someone who is simply following the rules they were taught.

52
00:03:20.110 --> 00:03:23.310
<v Speaker 1>It sounds harsh, but it's not meant as a moral insult.

53
00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:27.150
<v Speaker 1>It's a precise description of cognitive limitation.

54
00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:30.990
<v Speaker 1>Think about how an animal interacts with a physical space.

55
00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:40.510
<v Speaker 1>A beast encounters a physical barrier like a brick wall, but it doesn't understand the concept of architecture or property lines or the purpose of a house.

56
00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:42.710
<v Speaker 2>It just registers the physical stimulus.

57
00:03:42.710 --> 00:03:43.150
<v Speaker 1>Exactly.

58
00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:44.350
<v Speaker 1>It merely registers it.

59
00:03:44.350 --> 00:03:49.710
<v Speaker 1>If a human being only engages with the visible forms of their tradition, they're doing the exact same thing.

60
00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:52.510
<v Speaker 1>They're simply registering spiritual stimuli.

61
00:03:52.590 --> 00:03:58.030
<v Speaker 2>They memorize the shapes of the letters or the motions of the prayer, but entirely miss the architecture.

62
00:03:58.030 --> 00:03:58.310
<v Speaker 1>Yes.

63
00:03:58.990 --> 00:04:03.550
<v Speaker 1>They're trapped in a world of mere reaction, which is the defining characteristic of a beast.

64
00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:06.350
<v Speaker 2>Okay, that makes sense conceptually, but I have to push back here.

65
00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:07.790
<v Speaker 2>That sounds like clever wordplay.

66
00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:11.310
<v Speaker 2>Yeah, I mean, isn't this just relabeling 2 layers as three?

67
00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:15.070
<v Speaker 2>You have a visible action and you have the hidden intention behind it.

68
00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:20.670
<v Speaker 2>Asserting a third layer of the inner just feels like multiplying layers for poetic effect.

69
00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:23.070
<v Speaker 1>I completely understand why you'd argue that.

70
00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:27.550
<v Speaker 1>It's the natural skepticism of anyone looking at esoteric philosophy.

71
00:04:27.550 --> 00:04:30.430
<v Speaker 2>It sounds profound, but does it actually exist in reality?

72
00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:30.750
<v Speaker 1>Right.

73
00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:35.550
<v Speaker 1>It's very easy to assume that mystical texts just pile on layers to sound more profound or exclusive.

74
00:04:36.110 --> 00:04:40.030
<v Speaker 1>But the author anticipates this exact assumption and steel mans it.

75
00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:45.150
<v Speaker 1>He dismantles it completely by walking through three specific nested proofs

76
00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:47.630
<v Speaker 1>to show this triple structure isn't just poetry.

77
00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:52.950
<v Speaker 2>Okay, let's walk through those proofs then, because if this geometry is foundational, it should be universally applicable.

78
00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:53.470
<v Speaker 1>It is.

79
00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:58.830
<v Speaker 1>The first analogy uses a very tangible physical reality drawn directly from the Quran.

80
00:04:59.470 --> 00:05:03.390
<v Speaker 1>Specifically, chapter 7, verse 26, which discusses clothing.

81
00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:08.830
<v Speaker 1>When you break down the reality of what clothing is, you find 3 distinct layers that cannot be collapsed into two.

82
00:05:09.550 --> 00:05:11.310
<v Speaker 1>First, you have the physical fabric you wear.

83
00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:15.150
<v Speaker 2>The part that is visible to everyone, like the wool or the cotton.

84
00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:17.470
<v Speaker 1>Yes, that is the outer aspect.

85
00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:18.910
<v Speaker 1>But why do you wear it?

86
00:05:19.390 --> 00:05:23.710
<v Speaker 1>The verse moves to the second layer, which is the covering of what is private.

87
00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:24.830
<v Speaker 1>That's the inner aspect.

88
00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:27.350
<v Speaker 2>It's the function or the purpose of the visible fabric.

89
00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:27.870
<v Speaker 1>Exactly.

90
00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:32.830
<v Speaker 1>The fabric is merely serving a hidden necessity, which is modesty or the concealment of the body.

91
00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:35.470
<v Speaker 1>If you stop there, you have your two layers.

92
00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:37.950
<v Speaker 1>the fabric and the function of the fabric.

93
00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:42.990
<v Speaker 2>Which is usually where our everyday understanding stops, the action and the intention behind it.

94
00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:44.990
<v Speaker 1>But the verse doesn't stop there.

95
00:05:45.390 --> 00:05:48.270
<v Speaker 1>It introduces 1/3 layer, the garment of piety.

96
00:05:49.310 --> 00:05:54.430
<v Speaker 1>That is the absolute deepest spiritual principle toward which the physical clothing is merely pointing.

97
00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:55.950
<v Speaker 1>It is the inner of the inner.

98
00:05:55.950 --> 00:06:01.630
<v Speaker 1>It's the ultimate orientation of the soul that necessitates the modesty, which in turn necessitates the fabric.

99
00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:05.310
<v Speaker 2>So without the garment of piety, the covering becomes purely social.

100
00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:07.950
<v Speaker 2>And without the covering, the fabric becomes useless.

101
00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:08.590
<v Speaker 1>Precisely.

102
00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:12.590
<v Speaker 1>One verse, one everyday image, but three nested, indivisible meanings.

103
00:06:12.670 --> 00:06:13.790
<v Speaker 1>All 3 must exist.

104
00:06:14.030 --> 00:06:17.390
<v Speaker 2>That makes the mechanism incredibly clear for a physical object.

105
00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:22.590
<v Speaker 2>You move from the object to its immediate function to its ultimate spiritual root.

106
00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:25.790
<v Speaker 2>But what about outside of physical objects?

107
00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:27.870
<v Speaker 2>Like how we think and communicate?

108
00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:29.630
<v Speaker 1>That's where the second proof comes in.

109
00:06:30.190 --> 00:06:33.630
<v Speaker 1>It moves to the intellectual proof through the mechanism of grammar itself.

110
00:06:34.670 --> 00:06:37.790
<v Speaker 1>Take a simple three-word observation, the moon rose.

111
00:06:38.190 --> 00:06:39.150
<v Speaker 2>A standard sentence.

112
00:06:39.150 --> 00:06:41.710
<v Speaker 2>We use grammatical structures like that 100 times a day.

113
00:06:41.870 --> 00:06:45.350
<v Speaker 1>Yeah, but look at the invisible architecture of how we derive understanding from it.

114
00:06:45.950 --> 00:06:48.750
<v Speaker 1>The text breaks it down into 3 necessary pillars.

115
00:06:49.150 --> 00:06:50.430
<v Speaker 1>The word moon is the name.

116
00:06:50.830 --> 00:06:52.630
<v Speaker 1>The action rose is the attribute.

117
00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:56.190
<v Speaker 1>But the actual physical disk in the night sky

118
00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:59.950
<v Speaker 1>The celestial body itself is the meaning.

119
00:07:00.030 --> 00:07:01.790
<v Speaker 2>Okay, let me see if I can trace that logic.

120
00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:07.750
<v Speaker 2>If you just have the physical disc in the sky without a name, it is something seen but completely unnamable.

121
00:07:07.750 --> 00:07:09.470
<v Speaker 1>You couldn't communicate it to anyone else.

122
00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:10.110
<v Speaker 2>Precisely.

123
00:07:10.270 --> 00:07:16.030
<v Speaker 2>And if you have the name moon without the actual disc existing in reality, it is just a hollow sound with no reference point.

124
00:07:16.270 --> 00:07:22.110
<v Speaker 2>And the attribute rose without either the name or the meaning is just a verb hanging in empty space.

125
00:07:22.510 --> 00:07:26.430
<v Speaker 2>It signifies an action, but there's no actor and no subject.

126
00:07:26.510 --> 00:07:27.070
<v Speaker 1>You got it.

127
00:07:27.230 --> 00:07:29.790
<v Speaker 1>You need the signifier, the attribute, and the essence.

128
00:07:29.950 --> 00:07:32.270
<v Speaker 1>None of these three can function in isolation.

129
00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:38.030
<v Speaker 2>And so the text is mapping this grammatical necessity directly onto the structure of religion.

130
00:07:38.030 --> 00:07:38.750
<v Speaker 1>Exactly.

131
00:07:38.990 --> 00:07:42.670
<v Speaker 1>The literal words recited or physical actions performed are the name.

132
00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:52.190
<v Speaker 1>The spiritual states and functions those names point to in the believer's life are the attributes, and the innermost level is the true meaning, the divine essence.

133
00:07:52.430 --> 00:07:58.350
<v Speaker 2>You cannot collapse it into two, just as you can't have a sentence with only a noun and a verb, no underlying reality.

134
00:07:58.350 --> 00:07:59.870
<v Speaker 1>Okay, so we've done fabric and grammar.

135
00:08:00.110 --> 00:08:03.230
<v Speaker 2>Yeah, but language is man-made and clothing is man-made.

136
00:08:03.470 --> 00:08:06.990
<v Speaker 2>Does this triple layer structure exist organically in nature?

137
00:08:07.070 --> 00:08:10.190
<v Speaker 1>It does, and that brings us to the most biological proof in the text.

138
00:08:10.430 --> 00:08:12.110
<v Speaker 1>Picture an egg sitting on a table.

139
00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:15.710
<v Speaker 1>The text identifies the shell as the outer aspect.

140
00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:18.830
<v Speaker 2>The hard, visible exterior protecting what's inside.

141
00:08:18.990 --> 00:08:19.310
<v Speaker 1>Right.

142
00:08:19.790 --> 00:08:24.030
<v Speaker 1>Then you have the white, which is the inner aspect, the protective liquid layer sitting beneath the cover.

143
00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:25.630
<v Speaker 1>But finally, you have the yolk.

144
00:08:25.950 --> 00:08:27.550
<v Speaker 2>The yolk being the inner of the inner.

145
00:08:27.550 --> 00:08:28.750
<v Speaker 1>Yes, the innermost core.

146
00:08:28.950 --> 00:08:33.230
<v Speaker 1>It's the true substance, the biological center from which life actually originates.

147
00:08:33.710 --> 00:08:37.630
<v Speaker 1>Shell, white, yolk, outer, inner, innermost.

148
00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:39.310
<v Speaker 2>It's not a poetic choice.

149
00:08:40.070 --> 00:08:42.590
<v Speaker 2>structural necessity for life to exist.

150
00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:48.150
<v Speaker 1>If you remove any one of those layers, it ceases to be an egg and life cannot germinate.

151
00:08:48.150 --> 00:08:50.750
<v Speaker 1>And it's vital to ground this.

152
00:08:51.070 --> 00:08:55.550
<v Speaker 1>in its academic context because it shows how pervasive this thinking was.

153
00:08:55.550 --> 00:08:57.550
<v Speaker 2>It wasn't just an isolated metaphor.

154
00:08:57.550 --> 00:08:58.270
<v Speaker 1>Far from it.

155
00:08:58.270 --> 00:09:07.550
<v Speaker 1>Scholars like Henry Corbin in his work, Cyclical Time and Smiling Gnosis, point out that this triple structure is the architecture under which every single verse of scripture was read in this tradition.

156
00:09:07.630 --> 00:09:16.750
<v Speaker 2>And Anna-Ri Schimmel in Mystical Dimensions of Islam demonstrates that this exact same three-fold reading spans well beyond one specific circle.

157
00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:19.870
<v Speaker 1>Yeah, it reaches deeply into wider mystical traditions.

158
00:09:20.430 --> 00:09:30.910
<v Speaker 1>Corbin and Schimmel both confirm that the disciple is being inducted into a massive shared intellectual architecture that governed how entire civilizations understood reality.

159
00:09:30.910 --> 00:09:33.470
<v Speaker 2>And that brings us to the crucial pivot in the text.

160
00:09:33.550 --> 00:09:41.390
<v Speaker 2>We've established the structure of knowledge with the three layers, but how does this map onto the structure of who is doing the knowing, like we mentioned beasts earlier?

161
00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:43.710
<v Speaker 1>The mapping is a direct one-to-one sequence.

162
00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:46.510
<v Speaker 1>We said the outer aspect belongs to beasts.

163
00:09:46.510 --> 00:09:48.030
<v Speaker 1>They interact only with the shell.

164
00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:53.150
<v Speaker 1>The middle layer, the strictly human level of knowing, belongs to the true descendants of Adam.

165
00:09:53.270 --> 00:09:59.230
<v Speaker 2>That's the space where human consciousness actively engages with the inner meaning behind the visible world.

166
00:09:59.230 --> 00:10:01.070
<v Speaker 1>Yes, the space of Baden.

167
00:10:01.790 --> 00:10:03.870
<v Speaker 1>And the highest layer belongs to the angels.

168
00:10:04.110 --> 00:10:07.790
<v Speaker 1>This represents the rung of the prophets, the vice adjurants who are placed on Earth.

169
00:10:08.030 --> 00:10:09.710
<v Speaker 1>They operate at Baden al-Baten.

170
00:10:09.870 --> 00:10:15.310
<v Speaker 2>What is genuinely fascinating here is the cosmological context for why the ladder runs in this exact sequence.

171
00:10:15.310 --> 00:10:19.150
<v Speaker 2>Why does human intellect sit perfectly wedged between the beasts and the angel?

172
00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:23.150
<v Speaker 1>It feels like we need to understand the mechanism behind the ladder itself.

173
00:10:23.150 --> 00:10:23.510
<v Speaker 2>Yeah.

174
00:10:24.110 --> 00:10:29.150
<v Speaker 2>To understand that, we have to draw on the 10th century Fatimid thinker Al-Sijistani.

175
00:10:29.630 --> 00:10:37.630
<v Speaker 2>His profound cosmology, which has been beautifully reconstructed by modern scholar Khalil Andani, explains the origin of human thought.

176
00:10:37.750 --> 00:10:38.990
<v Speaker 1>It's a brilliant framework.

177
00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:39.710
<v Speaker 2>It really is.

178
00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:43.630
<v Speaker 2>In this framework, a God's creative act is not direct in the physical realm.

179
00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:46.270
<v Speaker 2>It is mediated through a first intellect.

180
00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:50.590
<v Speaker 2>So the intellect inside a human being isn't just a biological accident.

181
00:10:50.590 --> 00:10:54.670
<v Speaker 2>It's actually a trace, a direct remnant of that first intellect.

182
00:10:54.670 --> 00:11:00.270
<v Speaker 1>So human consciousness is literally a piece of the original creative force embedded in a physical form.

183
00:11:00.270 --> 00:11:00.910
<v Speaker 2>Exactly.

184
00:11:01.070 --> 00:11:03.310
<v Speaker 2>And this explains the entire purpose of the ladder.

185
00:11:03.470 --> 00:11:07.870
<v Speaker 2>Climbing the ladder is simply the mechanism of that trace turning back toward its origin.

186
00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:09.550
<v Speaker 1>Like a compass needle finding north.

187
00:11:09.630 --> 00:11:10.190
<v Speaker 2>Yes.

188
00:11:10.670 --> 00:11:14.990
<v Speaker 2>The beast level knower possesses the trace but leaves it pointed firmly at the ground.

189
00:11:15.550 --> 00:11:25.230
<v Speaker 2>The human level knower turns it inward toward the meaning, but the angelic level knower, the prophet, has turned that intellect all the way back toward its absolute divine origin.

190
00:11:25.390 --> 00:11:28.430
<v Speaker 1>That is why climbing the ladder is fundamentally an act of return.

191
00:11:29.150 --> 00:11:32.270
<v Speaker 2>And this raises a glaring, honestly uncomfortable question.

192
00:11:32.270 --> 00:11:36.670
<v Speaker 2>When you map humanity onto these rungs, doesn't it create a rigid caste system?

193
00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:43.230
<v Speaker 1>It sounds like a spiritual hierarchy that could easily justify leaving a vast majority of humanity behind in the dirt.

194
00:11:43.550 --> 00:11:48.750
<v Speaker 2>Are people permanently locked into thirds, beasts, humans, angels?

195
00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:55.070
<v Speaker 1>The text absolutely refuses to let this become a permanent sorting of mankind into rigid castes.

196
00:11:55.550 --> 00:12:00.110
<v Speaker 1>It clarifies that there are only two real human categories actively on this path.

197
00:12:00.190 --> 00:12:00.910
<v Speaker 2>Okay, what are they?

198
00:12:01.150 --> 00:12:06.430
<v Speaker 1>To explain this, it quotes the commander of the faithful, peace be upon him, from the peak of eloquence.

199
00:12:07.230 --> 00:12:10.750
<v Speaker 1>This comes from his deeply intimate advice to his student Kumail.

200
00:12:11.150 --> 00:12:16.030
<v Speaker 1>He says there is the sanctified scholar, the teacher whose spirit is firmly connected to certainty.

201
00:12:16.030 --> 00:12:17.110
<v Speaker 2>And the second category.

202
00:12:17.110 --> 00:12:17.790
<v Speaker 1>The seeker.

203
00:12:18.350 --> 00:12:21.470
<v Speaker 1>The learner who is actively walking upon the path of salvation.

204
